---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import evidence from '../../../corpus/tree-proofs.json';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
const optimization = evidence.optimization;
---
<section aria-label="Structural IR model evidence" class="structural-evidence">
  <p><span class="badge success">{evidence.proof.status}</span> <strong>p2_conditions structural IR model</strong></p>
  <p>{evidence.scope.domain} The independent specification requires pair-only acceptance and exact output <code>(1 . first(environment))</code>.</p>
  <ul>
    {evidence.proof.cases.map(check => <li><strong>{check.input_shape} environments:</strong> a solver-produced domain witness is replayed in native Rust, both Rust CLVM builds and independently compiled canonical Chialisp; no counterexample was found to the stated model obligation.</li>)}
    {evidence.mutations.map(mutation => <li><strong>{mutation.description}:</strong> {mutation.result.status}; {mutation.detected ? 'counterexample detected and replayed' : 'not detected'}.</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p>This proves the stated IR-model formulas under their encoded semantics. It does not prove rustc extraction, the model translator, CLVM lowering, all optimizer transformations, resource equivalence or consensus security.</p>
  <h3>Check the actual optimization</h3>
  <p><span class="badge success">{optimization.equivalence.status}</span> <strong>Before/after IR equivalence</strong>: equal rejection and successful output for both atom and pair environments. The rewritten program separately satisfies the independent factory specification.</p>
  <p>The typed-IR pass removes a redundant pair guard because a required checked projection still rejects atoms. These are proofs about this actual pair of expression trees, not every program the optimizer might receive.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>IR input</th><th>Compilation</th><th>Bytes</th><th>Published module</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{Object.entries(optimization.artifacts).flatMap(([kind, artifacts]) => artifacts.map(artifact => <tr><td>{kind === 'source' ? 'Source-derived' : 'Rewritten'}</td><td>{artifact.optimize ? 'Optimized' : 'Unoptimized'}</td><td>{artifact.bytes}</td><td>{artifact.clvm_hex === evidence.reference.clvm_hex && artifact.tree_hash === evidence.reference.tree_hash ? 'Exact bytes and hash' : 'Different'}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>Unsafe guard removal: {optimization.control.result.status}.</strong> The synthetic control replaces a guarded constant with an unconditional constant. Its atom witness rejects before the edit and accepts afterward in both VM optimization modes. The real pass keeps this guard.</p>
  <details><summary>Inspect the unsafe-rule counterexample</summary><div data-pagefind-ignore><Code code={JSON.stringify(optimization.control.counterexample, null, 2)} lang="json" /></div></details>
  <details><summary>Inspect the mutation witnesses</summary><div data-pagefind-ignore>{evidence.mutations.map(mutation => <div><p>{mutation.id}</p><Code code={JSON.stringify(mutation.counterexample, null, 2)} lang="json" /></div>)}</div></details>
  <details data-pagefind-ignore><summary>Download the {evidence.artifacts.length} IR and SMT artifacts</summary>
    <p>Exact report-listed original, rewritten and mutant IR, plus domain, specification and equivalence queries. Each file's SHA-256 is verified before the static site is built.</p>
    <ul>{evidence.artifacts.map(artifact => {
      const basename = artifact.path.split('/').at(-1)!;
      return <li><a href={href(`reports/structural/${basename}`)} download={basename}>{basename}</a> · <code class="structural-hash">{artifact.sha256}</code></li>;
    })}</ul>
  </details>
  <p><a href={href('reports/tree-proofs.json')}>Download the structural proof, source hashes, queries and replays →</a></p>
</section>
<style>
  .structural-evidence { border: 1px solid var(--oxide-line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.2rem; margin-block: 1.5rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; } li { margin-block: .5rem; }
  .structural-hash { overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: .7rem; }
</style>
